arXiv:2610.12234v2 Announce Type: replace 
Abstract: Recently, a uniform $\frac{7}{8}$ zero-free half-plane for finite-order Hecke $L$-functions over $\mathbb Q(\sqrt{-3})$ and its transfer to Dirichlet $L$-functions was given by OpenAI in [Ope26a]. In its proof, there are several parameters $b=\frac{1}{8}, \ell=\frac{1}{6}$, and $\kappa$. In this paper, via varying $b$, $\ell$, and $\kappa$, following the same strategy, we slightly improve the bound $\frac{7}{8}=0.875$ to \[
  B_{\mathrm{new}}=\frac{18\xi_{\mathrm{new}}+7}{18\xi_{\mathrm{new}}+9}
  =0.874957019420098946\ldots, \] where $\xi_{\mathrm{new}}$ is the unique root in $(0.38858,0.38859)$ of $1188\xi^3-2160\xi^2+171\xi+190=0$. Explicitly, with $\arccos\in[0,\pi]$, \[
  \xi_{\mathrm{new}}=\frac{20}{33}+\frac{\sqrt{1391}}{33}
  \cos\!\left(\frac13\arccos\frac{28470}{1391^{3/2}}
  -\frac{2\pi}{3}\right). \] The limiting parameters are \[ \begin{gathered}
  b_{\mathrm{new}}=\frac{8(3\xi_{\mathrm{new}}-1)(12\xi_{\mathrm{new}}^2-40\xi_{\mathrm{new}}+15)}
  {9(2\xi_{\mathrm{new}}+1)(24\xi_{\mathrm{new}}^2-20\xi_{\mathrm{new}}+5)},
  \ell_{\mathrm{new}}=\frac{5-6\xi_{\mathrm{new}}}{9+18\xi_{\mathrm{new}}},\qquad
  \kappa_{\mathrm{new}}=\frac{18\xi_{\mathrm{new}}+5}{18\xi_{\mathrm{new}}+9}
  =2B_{\mathrm{new}}-1. \end{gathered} \] We also prove its optimality within the explicitly specified exponent comparison system. This result has been formalized by Lean [Liu26].
